course: dictionary
lesson: 14156
title: Formal words in the news
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words belong to serious writing, like news reports, laws and business papers. Misstate is one of them. You do not need to be scared of it, because its meaning is close to a word you know well. «The newspaper misstated the final score, so the wrong team was named as the winner.» The clues are the score and the wrong team, so misstate must mean said or written wrongly.
explain: Misstate is a formal way of saying get wrong. It can happen by accident, when someone makes a mistake, or on purpose, when someone wants to fool people. «The witness misstated the time he saw the car.» We cannot tell from this sentence whether he forgot or lied, but the time he gave was still wrong.
explain: Look for the words around it. Facts, figures and numbers often sit next to misstate, as in «misstated figures». If you can swap in say wrongly and the sentence still makes sense, you have found the meaning.
fact: Misstate means to say or write something wrongly or falsely.
fact: You can misstate something by mistake or on purpose.
fact: Misstate is a formal word, often used in news, law and business.
fact: Everyday words for misstate are get wrong and say wrongly.
fact: Common phrases are «misstate the facts» and «misstated figures».
exercise: «The newspaper misstated the final score, so the wrong team was named as the winner.» What does misstate mean? | To run very fast to the finish | *To say something wrongly | To win a game by a large number of points | To say something very loudly
exercise: Which everyday phrase means the same as misstate? | Make a cake | *Get wrong | Forget the words of a song | Climb up high
exercise: Ruby says, «I misstated my age, but I didn't mean to lie.» Can you misstate something by accident? | *Yes, you can say something wrongly by mistake | Yes, but only in a song | No, misstate only means lying on purpose | No, it only means to stay silent
test: Which word is closest in meaning to misstate? | Draw neatly | *Say wrongly | Sleep soundly | Shout loudly
test: In which sentence is misstate used correctly? | I misstated my breakfast with a fork. | The sun misstated over the hill. | *The report misstated the number of people at the match. | My cat misstated the carpet with paint.
exam: Which statement about misstate is true? | *It means to say or write something wrongly or falsely, by mistake or on purpose | It means to clean something very carefully | It means to be very quiet and still | It means to be late for school
